'My proposed solution is to train an instance segmentation model from the YOLOv8 family, which is well-suited for this task. I will start by converting the provided `CellSegDataset` into the format required by YOLOv8 using the dataset's built-in helper function. Then, I will train a pre-trained `yolov8s-seg.pt` model on this data to leverage transfer learning, which should improve performance and reduce training time. After training is complete, I will use the best resulting model checkpoint to perform inference on the validation dataset images. For each validation image, I will process the model's output by combining the individual predicted masks into a single `uint16` instance mask, where each detected cell is assigned a unique integer ID. My goal is to maximize the mean Average Precision (mAP), a standard metric for instance segmentation that evaluates both the localization and segmentation quality of the predictions.'
