'My strategy is to leverage a state-of-the-art instance segmentation model, specifically `YOLOv8m-seg`, which provides a strong balance between performance and computational cost. I will substantially increase the training duration to 50 epochs and use a higher image resolution of 1024x1024 to better capture the fine details of the cells, which is critical for microscopy images. To prevent overfitting and optimize training time, I will employ an early stopping mechanism with a patience of 10 epochs. After training, the best-performing model checkpoint will be used to predict instance masks on the validation set. The final output masks will be generated by rendering the predicted segmentation polygons for each cell with a unique integer ID, and the model's performance will be evaluated using the standard mean Average Precision (mAP) metric for segmentation.'
