high-resolution microscopy data. I will employ the `yolov8l-seg` model, a larger and more capable architecture, to better learn the intricate features of the cells. To preserve crucial details, the training and inference image size will be increased to 1024x1024. The model will be trained for up to 80 epochs with an early stopping patience of 15, ensuring convergence without overfitting. For evaluation, I will use the standard mean Average Precision (mAP) for segmentation, and the final instance masks will be constructed by prioritizing higher-confidence predictions to resolve any overlaps.\nAnalysis: There is a critical bug in the execution. The provided code specifies using a large model (`yolov8l-seg.pt`), training at a high resolution (`imgsz=1024`), and for many epochs (`epochs=80`). However, the execution log shows that a much smaller nano model (`yolov8n-seg.pt`) was used, with a lower resolution (`imgsz=640`) and for only 2 epochs. This completely changes the intended experiment and leads to a low score. The fix is to ensure the execution environment runs the provided code without modification, using the specified large model and training hyperparameters.\n\n\n\n# Previous (buggy) implementation:\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport torch\nfrom ultralytics import YOLO\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml\nimport cv2\nfrom torch.utils.data import Dataset\nimport re\nfrom typing import Dict, List, Optional, Tuple\nimport tifffile\nimport warnings\nimport shutil\n\n# Ignore potential warnings from libraries\nwarnings.filterwarnings("ignore")\n\n# Assume the following classes and functions are pre-defined in the environment\n# as per the problem description.\n# --- Start of assumed pre-defined code ---\n\n\ndef _extract_index(name: str) -> Optional[int]:\n    """Tries to extract a trailing integer index from a filename stem."""\n    res = re.findall(r"(\\d+)$", name)\n    if not res:\n        return None\n    return int(res[0])\n\n\ndef _read_tif_any(p: Path) -> np.ndarray:\n    """Read a TIF file, handling various ways they are saved."""\n    img = tifffile.imread(p)\n    return img\n\n\ndef _as_rgb(img: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n    """Converts a 1-channel grayscale image to a 3-channel RGB image."""\n    if img.ndim == 2:\n        return np.stack([img] * 3, axis=-1)\n    if img.ndim == 3 and img.shape[-1] == 1:\n        return np.concatenate([img] * 3, axis=-1)\n    return img\n\n\ndef mask_to_yolo_and_iou(mask_path, txt_path, class_id=0):\n    """\n    This is a placeholder for the complex mask conversion logic.\n    In the actual benchmark environment, this function is provided.\n    It converts an instance mask to YOLO segmentation format.\n    """\n    mask = _read_tif_any(mask_path)\n    H, W = mask.shape\n    instance_ids = np.unique(mask)\n    instance_ids = instance_ids[instance_ids != 0]\n\n    with open(txt_path, "w") as f:\n        for inst_id in instance_ids:\n            inst_mask = mask == inst_id\n            contours, _ = cv2.findContours(\n                inst_mask.astype(np.uint8), cv2.RETR_EXTERNAL, cv2.CHAIN_APPROX_SIMPLE\n            )\n\n            if not contours:\n                continue\n\n            # Use the largest contour\n            contour = max(contours, key=cv2.contourArea)\n\n            if contour.shape[0] < 3:  # Need at least 3 points for a polygon\n                continue\n\n            points = contour.squeeze(1)\n\n            # Normalize coordinates\n            normalized_points = points.astype(np.float32)\n            normalized_points[:, 0] /= W\n            normalized_points[:, 1] /= H\n\n            line = f"{class_id} " + " ".join(\n                [f"{p[0]:.6f} {p[1]:.6f}" for p in normalized_points]\n            )\n            f.write(line + "\\n")\n\n    return 0.0, 0.0  # Placeholder return\n\n\nclass CellSegDataset(Dataset):\n    """\n    General-purpose segmentation dataset that pairs images and masks by numeric index.\n\n    Returns:\n        image: H x W x 3 (RGB)\n        mask:  H x W (uint16 instance IDs) OR None if require_masks=False and missing\n        meta:  dict with filename info\n    """\n\n    def __init__(\n        self,\n        data_dir,\n        ann_dir,\n        split: str = "train",\n        require_masks: bool = True,\n        image_glob: str = "*.tif",\n        mask_glob: str = "*.tif",\n    ):\n        self.data_dir = Path(data_dir)\n        self.ann_dir = Path(ann_dir)\n        self.split = split\n        self.require_masks = require_masks\n\n        self.img_dir = self.data_dir\n        self.mask_dir = self.ann_dir\n\n        img_paths = sorted(self.img_dir.glob(image_glob))\n        if not img_paths:\n            raise RuntimeError(f"No images found in {self.img_dir} (glob={image_glob})")\n\n        mask_paths = sorted(self.mask_dir.glob(mask_glob))\n        if not mask_paths and require_masks:\n            raise RuntimeError(f"No masks found in {self.mask_dir} (glob={mask_glob})")\n\n        img_by_idx: Dict[int, Path] = {}\n        for p in img_paths:\n            idx = _extract_index(p.stem)\n            if idx is None:\n                continue\n            img_by_idx[idx] = p\n\n        mask_by_idx: Dict[int, Path] = {}\n        for p in mask_paths:\n            idx = _extract_index(p.stem)\n            if idx is None:\n                continue\n            mask_by_idx[idx] = p\n\n        if not img_by_idx:\n            raise RuntimeError(\n                f"Found images in {self.img_dir} but none matched an index pattern (e.g., ...0000.tif)."\n            )\n\n        self.pairs: List[Tuple[int, Path, Optional[Path]]] = []\n        for idx in sorted(img_by_idx.keys()):\n            img_p = img_by_idx[idx]\n            m_p = mask_by_idx.get(idx, None)\n\n            if self.require_masks and m_p is None:\n                raise RuntimeError(\n                    f"Missing mask for image idx={idx}: image={img_p.name}. "\n                    f"Expected a mask with the same trailing index in {self.mask_dir} "\n                    f"(e.g., man_seg{idx:04d}.tif or mask{idx:04d}.tif)."\n                )\n\n            self.pairs.append((idx, img_p, m_p))\n\n        if not self.pairs:\n            raise RuntimeError("No (image, mask) pairs could be formed.")\n\n    def __len__(self):\n        return len(self.pairs)\n\n    def __getitem__(self, i):\n        idx, img_path, mask_path = self.pairs[i]\n        img = _read_tif_any(img_path)\n        img = _as_rgb(img)\n\n        mask = None\n        if mask_path is not None:\n            m = _read_tif_any(mask_path)\n            if m.ndim == 3:\n                m = m[..., 0]\n            mask = m.astype(np.uint16)\n\n        meta = {\n            "index": idx,\n            "image_id": img_path.stem,\n            "image_path": str(img_path),\n            "mask_path": str(mask_path) if mask_path is not None else None,\n        }\n        return img, mask, meta\n\n    def generate_yolo_dataset(\n        self,\n        yolo_dir: str | Path,\n        *,\n        class_id: int = 0,\n        class_name: str = "cell",\n        write_empty_labels: bool = True,\n    ) -> str:\n        yolo_dir = Path(yolo_dir)\n        split = self.split\n        yolo_image_dir = yolo_dir / "images" / split\n        yolo_label_dir = yolo_dir / "labels" / split\n        yolo_image_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n        yolo_label_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n        num_written = 0\n        for idx, img_path, mask_path in self.pairs:\n            assert img_path.exists(), f"Missing image: {img_path}"\n            img = _read_tif_any(img_path)\n            img = _as_rgb(img)\n            if img.dtype != np.uint8:\n                img = np.clip(img, 0, 255).astype(np.uint8)\n            out_img_name = f"{img_path.stem}.png"\n            out_img_path = yolo_image_dir / out_img_name\n            if not out_img_path.exists():\n                cv2.imwrite(str(out_img_path), cv2.cvtColor(img, cv2.COLOR_RGB2BGR))\n            label_path = yolo_label_dir / f"{img_path.stem}.txt"\n            if mask_path is not None and Path(mask_path).exists():\n                mask_to_yolo_and_iou(\n                    mask_path=mask_path,\n                    txt_path=label_path,\n                    class_id=class_id,\n                )\n            else:\n                if write_empty_labels:\n                    label_path.touch()\n                else:\n                    continue\n            num_written += 1\n        data_yaml_path = yolo_dir / "data.yaml"\n        yaml_config = {\n            "path": str(yolo_dir.resolve()),\n            "train": f"images/{self.split if self.split == \'train\' else \'../train\'}",\n            "val": f"images/{self.split if self.split == \'val\' else \'../val\'}",\n            "names": {class_id: class_name},\n        }\n        if data_yaml_path.exists():\n            try:\n                with open(data_yaml_path, "r") as f:\n                    existing = yaml.safe_load(f) or {}\n            except Exception:\n                existing = {}\n            existing.update(yaml_config)\n            yaml_config = existing\n        with open(data_yaml_path, "w") as f:\n            yaml.safe_dump(yaml_config, f, sort_keys=False)\n        self.yolo_dir = yolo_dir\n        self.yolo_yaml_path = str(data_yaml_path)\n        return str(data_yaml_path)\n\n\n# --- End of assumed pre-defined code ---\n\n\ndef cell_segmentation(\n    train_dataset: CellSegDataset, val_dataset: CellSegDataset\n) -> list[np.ndarray]:\n    """\n    Performs instance segmentation on a validation dataset of cell images.\n\n    This solution uses the YOLOv8-large segmentation model, trains it on a higher\n    resolution (1024x1024) for a longer duration with early stopping to achieve\n    high accuracy on detailed microscopy images. Post-processing handles\n    overlapping instances by prioritizing higher-confidence detections.\n\n    Args:\n        train_dataset: A CellSegDataset containing training images and masks.\n        val_dataset: A CellSegDataset containing validation images.\n\n    Returns:\n        A list of uint16 instance-id masks, one per image in val_dataset.\n    """\n\n    # 1. Setup workspace\n    yolo_dir = Path("./yolo_cell_dataset")\n    if yolo_dir.exists():\n        shutil.rmtree(yolo_dir)\n    yolo_dir.mkdir()\n\n    run_dir = Path("./yolo_runs")\n\n    # 2. Generate YOLO-compatible datasets\n    print("Generating YOLO dataset for training...")\n    # This call sets up the yaml file with the \'train\' path\n    data_yaml_path = train_dataset.generate_yolo_dataset(\n        yolo_dir=yolo_dir, split="train"\n    )\n\n    print("Generating YOLO dataset for validation...")\n    # This call updates the same yaml file with the \'val\' path\n    val_dataset.generate_yolo_dataset(yolo_dir=yolo_dir, split="val")\n\n    # 3. Train the model\n    # Use a larger model (yolov8l-seg) for better performance\n    model = YOLO("yolov8l-seg.pt")\n\n    print("Starting model training...")\n    # Train for more epochs, at higher resolution, with early stopping\n    results = model.train(\n        data=data_yaml_path,\n        epochs=80,\n        patience=15,\n        imgsz=1024,\n        project=str(run_dir),\n        name="cell_seg_l_1024",\n        device=0,\n        batch=16,\n        verbose=True,\n    )\n\n    # Print final validation metrics from the training logs\n    final_val_map = results.results_dict.get("metrics/mAP50-95(M)", 0.0)\n    print(f"Final validation mask mAP50-95 from training: {final_val_map}")\n    print(f"Validation Metric: {final_val_map}")\n\n    # 4. Perform inference on the validation set using the best model\n    best_model_path = results.save_dir / "weights" / "best.pt"\n    if not best_model_path.exists():\n        raise FileNotFoundError(f"Best model not found at {best_model_path}")\n    best_model = YOLO(best_model_path)\n\n    seg_mask_list = []\n    print(f"Performing inference on {len(val_dataset)} validation images...")\n\n    for i in range(len(val_dataset)):\n        img, _, _ = val_dataset[i]\n        H, W, _ = img.shape\n\n        # Predict on the image\n        preds = best_model.predict(\n            img, imgsz=1024, conf=0.25, verbose=False  # A common confidence threshold\n        )\n        result = preds[0]\n\n        # Create the final instance mask with robust overlap handling\n        final_mask = np.zeros((H, W), dtype=np.uint16)\n\n        if result.masks is not None and len(result.masks) > 0:\n            # Get confidences and sort detections by confidence in descending order\n            confs = result.boxes.conf.cpu().numpy()\n            sorted_indices = np.argsort(confs)[::-1]\n\n            masks = result.masks.masks.cpu().numpy()\n\n            instance_id = 1\n            for idx in sorted_indices:\n                mask = masks[idx]\n                # Ensure mask is resized to original image dimensions if not already\n                if mask.shape != (H, W):\n                    mask = cv2.resize(mask, (W, H), interpolation=cv2.INTER_NEAREST)\n\n                bool_mask = mask > 0.5\n\n                # Add the current mask, but only where the final mask is empty (0).\n                # This ensures higher-confidence masks are not overwritten by lower-confidence ones.\n                final_mask[bool_mask & (final_mask == 0)] = instance_id\n                instance_id += 1\n\n        seg_mask_list.append(final_mask)\n\n    print("Inference complete.")\n\n    # Clean up generated files\n    shutil.rmtree(yolo_dir)\n    # The run_dir contains the models, which might be useful, so we can leave it.\n\n    return seg_mask_list\n\n```\n\n# Execution output:\n```\n✅ Added /work to sys.path\nWorking dir: /\n✅ Added /work to sys.path\nWorking dir: /\n  program_path: /work/program.py (exists: True)\n[INFO] Loading program from /work/program.py\nWARNING ⚠️ user config directory \'/root/.config/Ultralytics\' is not writable, using \'/tmp/Ultralytics\'. Set YOLO_C